## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical understanding of cloud AI wiring, cost controls, and data safety in a beginner-friendly Azure setup.

## Key Concepts
- Azure OpenAI Service behind API Management
- Blob Storage for knowledge base
- Azure Cognitive Search for grounding
- PII redaction in input
- Per-tenant token-budget gate

## Code Example
```javascript
// Redaction example
function redactPII(text) {
  return text.replace(/\b\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}\b/g, "[REDACTED_DATE]");
}
```
```javascript
// Budget guard example
function withinBudget(nextTokens, budget, spent) {
  return spent + nextTokens < budget;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This probes governance at scale: per-tenant safety, data residency, and cost-aware routing in a live Azure OpenAI pipeline.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-aware policy packs in blob storage
- PDP (policy decision point) in Azure Functions
- Data residency routing to OpenAI regional endpoints
- Redaction and guardrails before outbound calls
- Auditing and observability via Azure Monitor

## Code Example
```javascript
function evaluatePDP(tenantId, metadata, policies) {
  const policy = policies[tenantId] || policies["default"];
  // residency check
  if (policy.residency && policy.residency !== metadata.region) return { action: "block" };
  // budget constraint
  if (typeof policy.budget === "number" && metadata.cost > policy.budget) return { action: "redirect", destination: "onPrem" };
  // allowed destination
  if (policy.allowedDestinations?.includes("OpenAI")) return { action: "allow", destination: "OpenAI" };
  return { action: "block" };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test PDP edge cases (missing tenant, malformed metadata, policy drift)?
- How would you implement zero-downtime policy updates and per-tenant rollbacks?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to integrate AI into CI/CD for policy enforcement, including per-tenant RBAC, versioned knowledge bases, and auditable logs.

## Key Concepts

- IaC and manifest static analysis with OpenAI prompts
- Versioned KB in Azure Blob + Cognitive Search queries
- Per-tenant RBAC via Azure AD
- Automated remediation guidance and risk scoring
- Auditable run logs stored in Data Lake and surfaced in PR checks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Node-like pseudocode: extractFiles -> prompt -> OpenAI -> outputRemediation()
async function auditFiles(files, kbVersion) {
  const insights = await openai.promptAnalyze({ files, kbVersion });
  const remediations = generateRemediation(insights);
  await storeAuditLog({ files, remediations, kbVersion });
  return remediations;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle KB versioning across multi-tenant tenants to avoid leakage?
- What metrics would you surface in dashboards to indicate compliance drift over time?
- How would you integrate this with multiple CI systems (GitHub Actions, Azure Pipelines)?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to architect a governance-heavy, production-ready OpenAI integration across tenants, including data redaction, KB grounding, per-tenant state, and actionable remediation.

## Key Concepts
- Azure OpenAI moderation and content safety
- Text Analytics for redaction
- Cognitive Search KB grounding with versioning
- Cosmos DB per-tenant state
- Azure Boards for remediation/workflow
- Canary deployments and end-to-end auditing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-pipeline orchestration sketch
async function evaluate(tp) {
  const moderated = await mod.check(tp.prompt, tp.response);
  const redacted = redactor.redact(moderated);
  const grounded = kb.ground(redacted, tp.tenantId);
  const risk = riskStore.update(tp.tenantId, grounded.score);
  board.createTask(tp.tenantId, risk, grounded.details);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement tenant isolation and key management to prevent data leaks across tenants?
- What metrics and alerting would you introduce to detect degradation or drift in evaluation quality?

